title: Coalition Affairs
subtitle: While PPS sits in the cabinet: raise a demand in the Council of Ministers, give way to our partners, or leave.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.coalitionCardAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card government.coalition_affairs (Z — 0.64, decisions 1A–3A of 7 X 2026; technical reference 9.8, card catalogue 7.6):
// the card of card 7.6 for a PPS member of the cabinet, in the Government deck. It has the rhythm of the support card
// (half a year, or at once after an act of the cabinet against PPS) and uses its options, worded for a coalition, and adds
// the concession to the partners. An ordinary use costs this month's action; opening and closing the card are free.
Q.pl_sup_mode = 'ordinary';
Q.pl_sup_reason = PolishGovernment.supportReason(Q);
Q.pl_sup_member = 1;
Q.pl_sup_withdraw_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'withdraw', 'ordinary').reason;
Q.pl_sup_demand_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', 'ordinary').reason;
Q.pl_sup_military_reason = PolishGovernment.supportOptionStatus(Q, 'bargain', 'ordinary', 'military_compromise').reason;
Q.pl_coal_tension = PolishGovernment.coalitionTensionText(Q);
Q.pl_coal_concession_reason = PolishGovernment.concessionStatus(Q).reason;
!}

= Coalition affairs

[? if pl_sup_reason : [+ pl_sup_reason +] ?]

Prime minister: [+ prime_minister_display +]. PPS position: [+ pps_government_position +].

[? if pl_cabinet_support_display : Declared support: [+ pl_cabinet_support_display +]. ?]

[? if pl_coal_tension : [+ pl_coal_tension +] ?]

Our ministers sit in the Council of Ministers with our partners. **An ultimatum** makes our demand a condition of staying in the cabinet: if the partners refuse, we must either leave or back down. **A proposal** asks without a threat and costs no relations. **Giving way** to the partners eases the tension in our coalition agreements, but the Left of PPS dislikes it.

- @polish_government_support.bargain
- @polish_government_support.persuade
- @polish_government_support.bargain_military
- @polish_government_support.persuade_military
- @concession
- @polish_government_support.withdraw
- @easy_discard

@concession
title: Give way to our coalition partners
subtitle: The tension in each of our coalition agreements falls by 20; the Left of PPS is displeased (+5 dissent).
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.concessionStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coal_concession_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.coalitionConcession(Q);
Q.pl_coal_tension = PolishGovernment.coalitionTensionText(Q);
!}
go-to: conceded

@conceded
new-page: true

= We give way

PPS lets the partners have their way on the disputed points. [+ pl_coal_tension +] The Left of PPS sees it as a retreat.

- @root: Continue.
